# Toolbar icons — Tabler only (Steve)

**Every toolbar, sidebar rail, dock, popover, and UI chrome icon must come from [Tabler Icons](https://tabler.io/icons)** — outline 24×24, stroke 2, `class="toolbar-icon"`.

## Allowed icon source (sole)

| Source | How |
|---|---|
| **`src/components/sceneToolbar/SceneToolbarIcons.jsx`** | Export named `Icon*` component with SVG from Tabler · pattern: `<svg class="toolbar-icon" xmlns="..." width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" strokeWidth="2" strokeLinecap="round" strokeLinejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" {...props}>` + paths |

## Strictly forbidden

- ❌ `react-icons` (any package — `fa`, `md`, `fi`, `io`, `io5`, `bi`, etc.)
- ❌ Emoji as UI controls (🏥, ➕, ❌, ✓, etc.)
- ❌ Custom hand-drawn SVG outside the Tabler spec
- ❌ New icon npm packages
- ❌ Inline data-URI SVG that isn't a Tabler path

## When you need a new icon

1. Search https://tabler.io/icons for the concept
2. Copy the SVG `path` elements (no `<svg>` wrapper — use the template pattern)
3. Export as `IconCamelName` in `SceneToolbarIcons.jsx`
4. Import and use: `<IconCamelName />` with `className="toolbar-icon"`

## Why

- Tabler was chosen because it's consistent, open-source, and already threaded through every toolbar button in the game
- Mixing icon sets (react-icons, emoji, hand-drawn) creates visual noise that breaks the UI coherence
- The toolbar-icon CSS class (`scene-toolbar.css`) depends on Tabler's outline/stroke-2 format for correct sizing, hover, and active-state coloring
